{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795613454,"nonce":"wQVa6nXM34gFsuJuWKD0WbxSbyw=","title":"Runs of a rich text in different faces draw on different baselines","message":"A `RichText` with bold or italic words draws them a pixel above the regular text beside them. Each run is centred on the line by its own face's ascent and descent, which differ between the regular, bold and italic faces. The rich text editor has the same fault in a line with inline code, where the body runs were offset as one face.\n\nReproducer: `rich_text(\"nnnn\u003cb\u003ennnn\u003c/b\u003e\u003ci\u003ennnn\u003c/i\u003e\")` at 15 px and 1x scale, and read the last inked row of each run.\n\nThe underline of a text positioned by its baseline also leaves out the half-leading that the glyphs are drawn with.","files":null}]}